# Copy this file to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in real values.
# Only the Google Places key is documented here; other public client IDs and
# Firebase config live in app.json (they are public by design). The native
# Google Maps SDK key for Android lives in app.json's android.config.googleMaps
# (KIN-122) — not here, and not in .env — because app.config.js used to inject
# it from this file, which made the resolved Expo config non-deterministic:
# with runtimeVersion on the "fingerprint" policy, whether this var was set in
# a given build environment changed the computed runtimeVersion itself. The key
# is not a secret in the way an API secret is — prebuild writes it straight into
# AndroidManifest.xml and it ships inside the APK either way; what protects it
# is the application restriction (package + SHA-1) in Google Cloud Console, not
# keeping it out of the repo.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Places + Geocoding (client web calls: Place Autocomplete/Details, Geocoding)
# Cloud Console → API restriction: "Places API" + "Geocoding API" only.
# Application restriction: none possible for mobile web calls — protect with
# per-key quotas + billing alerts. NOTE: EXPO_PUBLIC_* is inlined into the app
# bundle, so this key still ships in the app; the API restriction + quotas
# are what limit abuse. (A server-side proxy would remove it from the client.)
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=
